From 3efb82ef0848c234d3b5b2ab1e0e8f00b17db72e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Macready <william.macready@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:58:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] test(jax): single-layer transformer through Lean and JAX

Adds example 12's one-layer transformer (non-identity weights, SEQ=3 D=4 H=2 K=2 DFF=4, causal mask keeping 1/2/3 entries) as a fixture of the nonlinearity differential in both precisions. The Lean driver pins the plan shape (10 assign / 1 pointwise / 3 axiswise, 14 steps) and the verifier compares every materialized output within the unchanged tolerances, eager and jit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
